
sort filename  --> to sort in alphabetical order


sort -r filename  --> sort in reverse alphabetical order


sort names.txt -o sorted.txt    --> sort and save to another file


sort -n numbers.txt         --> sort numeric numbers


sort -nr numbers.txt        --> sort numeric numbers in reverse order


sort -f fruits.txt          --> case insensitive


sort -k2,2 filename         --> Sort by the second field (name)


sort -k3,3n employees.txt    --> Sort by the third field numerically (salary)


sort -k3,3nr employees.txt   --> Sort by salary from highest to lowest


sort -t',' -k2,2 employees.csv    --> Sort by the second comma-separated field, The -t',' option sets the comma as the field separator.


sort -t',' -k3,3nr employees.csv  --> Sort by salary in descending numeric order, The -t',' option sets the comma as the field separator.


sort -M months.txt    --> Month sorting


sort -V versions.txt   --> Version sorting




===========================================================


Note: sorr is mandatory for uniq


sort filename | uniq     --> remove duplicates


sort filename | uniq -c   --> count


sort filename | uniq -d   --> show only repeated/duplicate line


sort filename | uniq -u   --> Display only non-repeated lines


sort filename | uniq -i   --> Ignore case differences






